From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/50] ASoC: q6afe-dai: declare DISPLAY_PORT_RX as an input
 widget

DISPLAY_PORT_RX is a receive port: PCM arrives from a front-end mixer and
leaves the DSP towards the display.  Every other receive port in this file is
declared with SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN and only the transmit ports use
SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT:

  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("HDMI_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("SLIMBUS_0_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("QUAT_MI2S_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("SLIMBUS_0_TX", ...)

DISPLAY_PORT_RX is declared as an output, which is inconsistent with the
playback route that feeds it ("DISPLAY_PORT_RX Audio Mixer" ->
"DISPLAY_PORT_RX" in q6routing, "DISPLAY_PORT_RX" ->
"DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 Playback" in this file).  While here, pass NULL instead of
the string "NULL" for the stream name, like the neighbouring receive ports.

Note for v7.0.0-sm8150: this is a consistency fix, not a functional one.  The
DAPM core no longer derives power state from the AIF direction - aif_in and
aif_out widgets both use dapm_generic_check_power(), are not endpoints and sit
in the same power-up/down sequence groups (sound/soc/soc-dapm.c).  It does not
and cannot explain the "AFE enable for port 0x6020 failed -110" timeout.

Source: hotdog-linux-bringup 0052-asoc-q6afe-dai-make-displayport-a-playback-widget.patch
from the tree at github.com/Sr-0w/hotdog-linux-bringup, revision 47087509c428,
under aports/device/testing/linux-oneplus-hotdog-mainline616/.

Signed-off-by: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
index 0f47aad..aa9ca53 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -958,7 +958,7 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget q6afe_dai_widgets[] = {
 						0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("QUIN_TDM_TX_7", NULL,
 						0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("DISPLAY_PORT_RX", "NULL", 0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("DISPLAY_PORT_RX", NULL, 0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
 
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("WSA_CODEC_DMA_RX_0", "NULL",
 		0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
